  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Uganda &#x2013; investment in local agricultural processing</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With a DGGF Start-up loan Fiber Foods Holding B.V. will be able to set up a new jackfruit processing facility in Uganda together with their local partner Enimiro Products Uganda Ltd. Fiber Foods is active in sourcing and processing jackfruit in Uganda. They sell dehydrated jackfruit products to the food producing industry in The Netherlands and Europe mainly as a plant-based ingredient and alternative to meat.Jackfruit is a fruit that grows from shadow trees on fields for vanilla and coffee of smallholder farmers. The trees and fruits are abundantly available and farmers receive an additional income for selling their jackfruit. Jackfruit is a water and nutrient efficient crop and grows year-round. Previously, it was a non-commercial crop used as nutritious cover crops and additional (snack) food for children. Fiber Foods currently sources jackfruit from 1,300 trained and certified smallholder farmers of which 30% are women. This will be expanded to 3,000 smallholder farmers in the coming years.The estimated impact on local employment is the creation of approx. 450 direct and 1,500 indirect jobs, and knowledge transfer by training their employees and partners.</narrative>
  </description>
